From: NeoDarwin
Subject: [PATCH] ldi_vnode: don't read the ldi buf after starting asynchronous I/O

buf_strategy_vnode() reread lbp->b_iodone after VNOP_STRATEGY() to tell
synchronous I/O from asynchronous. An asynchronous buf's completion
(ldi_vnode_io_intr(), then vdev_disk_io_intr()) can run on another CPU
before that read, and lbp is zio->macos.zm_buf: once the zio is done and
freed, the next zio_create() zeroes it. The reread then saw b_iodone NULL
and treated the I/O as synchronous: buf_biowait() on a buf already freed
slept for good, holding a vdev_disk taskq thread, so `zpool import`
waited in spa_ld_verify_logs -> dmu_objset_find_dp -> taskq_wait past
SIGKILL (zpool_import_012_pos, P3-01 checkpoint 2; nd_threaddump showed
buf_biowait < buf_strategy_vnode < vdev_disk_io_strategy and the reads
under zil_parse in zio_wait). Before patch 0008 the same race freed the
buf twice (free_io_buf: bufs_iobufinuse < 0). Whether the I/O is
synchronous, and whether it writes, is now decided before it starts.

Rebase-risk: low
---
diff --git a/module/os/neodarwin/zfs/ldi_vnode.c b/module/os/neodarwin/zfs/ldi_vnode.c
--- a/module/os/neodarwin/zfs/ldi_vnode.c
+++ b/module/os/neodarwin/zfs/ldi_vnode.c
@@ -601,6 +601,21 @@
 		/* Does not return an error status */
 		vnode_startwrite(LH_VNODE(lhp));
 	}
+
+#ifdef __NEODARWIN__
+	/*
+	 * Decide now whether the I/O is synchronous: once VNOP_STRATEGY()
+	 * has started an asynchronous one, its completion
+	 * (ldi_vnode_io_intr(), then lbp->b_iodone) can run on another
+	 * CPU at any moment and release lbp, so lbp mustn't be read after
+	 * it. Rereading lbp->b_iodone found it zeroed by a new zio and
+	 * waited in buf_biowait() on a buf already freed, for good
+	 * (zpool import hung in the OpenZFS test suite), or, before patch
+	 * 0008, freed the buf twice (bufs_iobufinuse < 0).
+	 */
+	const boolean_t synchronous = (lbp->b_iodone == NULL);
+	const boolean_t is_write = !(lbp->b_flags & B_READ);
+#endif
 
 	/* Issue the IO, preserving error */
 	error = VNOP_STRATEGY(bp);
@@ -609,7 +624,11 @@
 		dprintf("%s VNOP_STRATEGY error %d\n",
 		    __func__, error);
 		/* Reclaim write count on vnode */
+#ifdef __NEODARWIN__
+		if (is_write) {
+#else
 		if (!(lbp->b_flags & B_READ)) {
+#endif
 			vnode_writedone(LH_VNODE(lhp));
 		}
 		vnode_put(LH_VNODE(lhp));
@@ -621,7 +640,16 @@
 	vnode_put(LH_VNODE(lhp));
 
 	/* For synchronous IO, call completion */
+#ifdef __NEODARWIN__
+	/*
+	 * Not lbp->b_iodone: an asynchronous buf's completion may already
+	 * have run, and its lbp (zio->macos.zm_buf) been freed and zeroed
+	 * by the next zio_create().
+	 */
+	if (synchronous) {
+#else
 	if (lbp->b_iodone == NULL) {
+#endif
 #ifdef __NEODARWIN__
 		/*
 		 * VNOP_STRATEGY() only starts the I/O: wait for it before
